    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δνοπᾰλ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shake violently, fling down,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ἄνδρ᾽ ἐδνοπάλιζεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.472
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σὰ ῥάκεα δνοπαλίξεις</span>
				'<i>wrap</i> thy old cloak <i>about thee</i>', <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.512
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυῖα δνοπαλίζεται,</span> of
			the polypus, its arms <i>wave about,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.295
			</span></i>.</div>
